Moving the 1-4-bit packer back in the pipeline #21626 introduced an issue where the `ht_done_pulse_i` can go high 1 cycle too early. This in combination with some other recent changes caused some unwanted words to be absorbed by SHA3.

When `ht_done_pulse_i` goes high this causes `process_i` for SHA3 to go high, which in turn leads to SHA3 not accepting any new inputs. If these signals go high 1 cycle too early SHA3 doesn't absorb the last word. The result were some test sequences that were failing due to a mismatch in the produced seeds.

I only observed it happening for the single lane mode, where one of the 4 random bit lanes is selected. This might be because the `post_ht` FIFO still receives the entropy without delay in normal operation.

Unfortunately I can't post a failing seed here for the `entropy_src_rng` test, since I had to change a lot in the DV environment to discover this bug.
